&00&03A crop of maize has been planted in this part of the field, and appears to be maturing quite well.&00~
   Maize stems superficially resemble bamboo canes.  Maize has a very distinct
growth form; the lower leaves being like broad flags, the stems are erect with
many nodes, casting off flag-leaves at every node.  Under these leaves and
close to the stem grow the ears.    
~
