barley stalk crop grain~
   Next to wheat the most valuable grain is barley, especially on light and
sharp soils.  It is a tender grain and easily hurt in any of the stages of its
growth, particularly at seed time; a heavy shower of rain will then almost ruin
a crop on the best prepared land; and in all the after processes greater pains
and attention are required to ensure success than in the case of other grains.
  
~
