barley ear~
   The barley ear must have its fibrous outer hull removed before it can be
eaten.  Once the grain has had the inedible hull removed, it is called dehulled
barley.  At this stage, the grain still has its bran and germ, which are
nutritious.  Although it could be eaten, this grain is also used in making many
types of beer and whiskey.    
~
