E
fountain statue water~
   The fountain is actually built into the ground within the center.  The edges
of the fountain are of white marble, and the stone beneath it is a deep blue.
In the center of the fountain stands an eight foot statue of the Chishan Chief.
Within the chiefs right hand is a sword held high as if to initiate battle.  
In her left hand rests a bowl, and it is within this bowl that the water
circulates from the fountain and overflows back in.  A soft flowing of water
can be heard as the water trickles through the bowl and splashes back into the
fountain.  At the edge of the fountain is an enscription:

&14"Proudly we shall stand together in the torment of adversity, and in the serenity&00
&14of peace."&00
~
